 "open_questions": [
  "POWER net class (VBUS, +5V): 1.0 mm traces and 0.8/0.4 mm vias are estimates; the trace width for the 3.5 A limit is not checked against a current-capacity source.",
  "TPS2121 IN2 tied to IN1; C2/C3 values estimated; RS-485 termination value open; no TVS or fuse on the bus input (see the blocks).",
  "Only the 40-pin socket is on the back; everything else is on top, so nothing sits over the Pi's own parts.",
  "Attachments: the Pi Zero 2 W, camera and cable are drawn from Raspberry Pi's drawings; the Pi's parts' heights, both boards' thickness and colours, the lens (retailer's 39 x 50 mm, layout from Raspberry Pi's lens guide illustration) and the C-CS adapter's size are estimates (see footprints/models/make.py).",
  "Attachments' finishes (metallic, roughness) and the lens's rib count, hood steps, glass and screw sizes are estimates from Waveshare's product photos; the lens printing's places are measured off its side-on photo."
 ],
